# Patch 0938 (wish of DevJunior, 19.11.2026: "the pick-ups of the remake, so you do not stop so much on your way";
# later "ammunition, treasures, grenades and general items, not weapons" and "the short version of the name: Handgun
# Ammo (amount)"). Not a bug of the prototype: a port feature of the mods (with the app's "Remake movement").
# game/sce_at.cpp sceAtFunc_item: money, treasures and what sceAtGetItem takes as it is (types 0, 4, 5, 7, 0xC),
# grenades (0x01, 0x02, 0x0E), weapon parts and the ammunition and healing items the case takes by itself (PutInCase)
# are taken at once, without the zoom and the question. The message: the item's short name cut from the game's own
# question 0x13 in the language played ("Handgun Ammo (10)"; the count for ammunition, else when more than one),
# shown through a one-message table in MesData file 4; money its own 0x14; the game's "obtained" 0x15 when the
# question has nothing to cut. It shows without stopping the game for 45 frames (a no-stop message lasts one frame:
# set again every frame; none during a remake call, patch 0939); the clean-up is sceAtGetItem's (sceAtQuickItemTask,
# a free scenario slot: two pick-ups in a row). Guns, keys, gems, files and a full case stay the game's.
